                                             "The reason people yearn to be an emperor is that it allows them to satisfy their desires for both the senses and the convenience that suits them.",
                                             "People today consider pavilions and towers to be beautiful, but the beams of Yao1鈥檚 dwelling were left unprocessed, and the rafters and columns were not adorned. Rare and exquisite delicacies are highly sought after by everyone, yet Yao ate coarse rice and drank wild vegetable soup. Bright-colored silks and expensive furs are favored by all, but Yao wore simple cloth to cover his body and used cheap deer skin to keep warm.",
                                             "Yao did not increase the things used for maintaining his health at all; instead, what grew was hisconcern for greater matters. Therefore, he passed the throne to Shun2, not merely out of the virtue of humility, but because he understood that beyond the heavy burdens, the position of emperor held nothing worth coveting. This is an example of how the power of the emperor was regarded with indifference."
