                                             "When Yao governed the world, he did not hanker after the wealth of the land or enjoy the position of emperor. He believed that the common people often fought with military force, with the strong bullying the weak, and the many harming the few.",
                                             "At this point, Yao personally advocated for frugality as a way to express his compassionate care for the people, thereby promoting harmony among the people across the land.",
                                             "Therefore, the thatched house where Yao lived was left untrimmed, the oak beams were not shaved, the large carts were not decorated, the reed mats were not even scissored at the edges, the soup was not seasoned with flavors, and the grains in the staple food were not ground. He traveled across the land to promote education, working hard for the people, having visited the Five Great Mountains3. Could it be that Yao鈥檚 treatment couldn鈥檛 provide him with enjoyment? For the whole world to revere him in such a manner would be detrimental.",
                                             "As Yao grew old and weak, troubled in his heart, he passed the entire realm to Shun, as effortlessly as retreating in walk or removing his shoes."
