                             "english":  [
                                             "Long ago, Gun1built city walls nine-ren2 high, yet the vassal lords rebelled against himand people beyond the seas grew alienated and disloyal. When Yu perceived that the world was on the verge of revolt, he demolished the walls, filled the moats, distributed wealth to the people, destroyed weapons as well as armorand bestowed kindness and virtue upon the populace. Thus, foreign tribes overseas renewed their allegianceand regional lords from all directions offered tribute. At the assembly of those lords beneath Mount Tu Shan, tens of thousands of states presented jade and silk.",
                                             "Therefore, if deceitful intentions lurk within, even the purest white will be deemed impure and wholehearted virtue will seem incomplete. How can one who fails to understand their own nature attract distant peoples?Sturdy armor breeds sharper weapons; towering walls inspire battering rams. Pouring boiling water to extinguish flames only worsens the chaos.Whipping a biting dog or subduing a kicking horse with crops-even with sage ministers like Yi Yin3 or master charioteers like Zao Fu4-will never truly tame them.Should the desire to harm others vanish, even a starving tiger could be followed safely, let alone mere dogs and horses.Thus, those who follow the great truth find ease without exhaustion, while manipulators of tactics toil without achievement."
                                         ],
