                                             "In ancient times, when Huang Di governed the land, he was assisted by two ministers, Li Mu1 and Tai Shan Ji2. He governed according to the laws of the sun and moon鈥檚 movements, establishing rules based on the changes of Yin-yang.",
                                             "Huang Di adjusted terms for the seasonal changes and set the standards for the lunar calendar. He abolished mixed living arrangements for men and women, assigning different responsibilities to each gender. He clarified the hierarchy of authority, distinguishing between the high and the low. He ensured that the strong did not bully the weak, and that those with greater numbers did not oppress those with fewer resources.",
                                             "Thanks to Huang Di鈥檚 governance, the people became skilled in maintaining health, allowing them to live long lives, and the crops matured without famine. The officials were just and impartial, with coordination between upper and lower ranks, free from resentment. The laws and regulations were clear and strict, and the assisting ministers were just, not flattery-driven.",
                                             "Farmers did not encroach on others鈥?land, and fishermen did not compete for the best fishing spots. Lost items on the road were not taken by others, and there were no deceptive market prices. The city gate did not need to be closed, and even remote villages had no thieves. Travelers on the border areas shared their possessions with one another. Even pigs and dogs did not fight over food left on the road.",
                                             "In this situation, the light of the sun and moon was clear and bright, and the stars did not deviate from their orbits. Winds and rains arrived according to the seasons, and the whole grains had a bountiful harvest every year. Tigers and wolves did not bite indiscriminately, and fierce birds did not hunt recklessly. Phoenixes perched in courtyards, and qilin3 roamed freely in the fields. The divine dragon presented a carriage to Huang Di, while the heavenly horses flew swiftly to serve him. Even in the distant northern states, such as Zhu Beiand Dan Er, there was no place that did not offer its tributes. Yet, despite all this, it still could not surpass the governing principles of Fu Xi4.",
                                             "Li Mu is a virtuous minister from ancient Chinese legends. According to the Records of the Grand Historian, he assisted Huang Di in governing the world, established policies and laws.",
                                             "Tai Shan Ji is believed to be the teacher of Huang Di and the ancestor of the Ji family, he is primarily documented in the Four Political Treatises of the Yellow Emperor.",
                                             "Qilin is a mythical beast in ancient Chinese mythology. Along with the 鈥渄ragon鈥? 鈥減hoenix, 鈥渢ortoise鈥?and 鈥減i xiu鈥? Qilin is considered one of the five great auspicious beasts.",
                                             "Fu Xi is a significant figure in ancient Chinese mythology, revered as one of the cultural ancestors of the Chinese nation. According to legend, Fu Xi is one of the Three Sovereigns of ancient times"
