                                             "Yu the Great went on an inspection tour to the south. As he was crossing the Yangtze River, a yellow dragon appeared in the water, carrying a small boat on its back. The people in the boat were terrified. But Yu just smiled and said cheerfully, 鈥淚 have received the mandate from the Heavenly Emperor and am doing my utmost to care for the people. My life is but a temporary stay in this world, and death is simply a return to my true home鈥攈ow could you disturb the harmony of Heaven?鈥?He regarded the yellow dragon as no more than a lizard, showing no change in his expression. The yellow dragon then drooped its ears, wagged its tail, and fled. To Yu, even a colossal creature was nothing more than a tiny being."
