                                             "The orangutan knows the past but not the future; the magpie knows the future but not the past鈥攅ach has its own strengths and weaknesses. In former times, the grand officer Chang Hong served the Zhou royal house as a specialist in calendrical calculations. He was thoroughly versed in the yin and yang of Heaven and Earth, the movements of the sun and moon, the transformations of wind and rain, and the methods of pitch-pipes and calendars; yet he could not foresee his own fate and died with his belly cut open. Su Qin, born a commoner, wearing leather shoes and carrying his baggage, traveled among the feudal lords and brought them to compliance and assent, yet in the end he could not escape being torn apart by chariots. King Yan of Xu treated the people with benevolence and personally practiced a government of humaneness and righteousness; thirty-two states came by land to pay him homage, yet in the end he died, his state was destroyed, and not even his descendants or clan survived."
